    <comment>At storm snow interface - CTE6 &amp;amp; CTM11 RP @ 61. IN FC above Nov RC - CTM19 SC@30 and CTH23 PC@29.

Limited new na av obs in the last week. Two snowfalls  first was 10cm Dec 28 and second -Jan 01 = 3cm. Winds predominantly from N/ NW light with minor new snow redistribution. HS variable from scoured to 200+cm in lee aspect terrain features.

ALP - HSL over various mid and basal FC layers.  TL - some specific locations with WSL over mid &amp;amp; basal FC layers.  BTL - HST over FC to ground.  

1 sz 1 Loose av on nigel bench triggered from the top by people who walked up there. 20cm Deep, 5 m wide, 30m long. stopped on rocks just above ditch.

Previous Wx: seaonal norms for temp, light N/NW winds sitting under a High

Forecasted WX: warmer temps and light snowfall that continues to get pushed back a day or two at a time.

ALP - Consid, TL - Mod, BTL - Low

F/G/G</comment>
